    uniqueContent: "Arlington is Northern Virginia's most urban county, and its housing reflects that density. The Rosslyn-Ballston corridor and the areas around Crystal City and Pentagon City are stacked with high-rise condominiums, while contemporary townhomes, Colonial-style single-family homes, garden apartments, and mixed-use residential buildings fill neighborhoods like Lyon Village, Nauck, and Shirlington. That mix shapes how we clean: a high-rise condo in Ballston might run 700 to 1,200 square feet on a single floor, whereas a Colonial single-family home in Lyon Village can stretch to 2,500 square feet or more across multiple levels. Our background-checked, bonded, and insured teams carry EPA Safer Choice, plant-based products that handle both a sleek new condo finish and a family home with hardwood and carpet.\n\nAs a size-based estimate, a typical three-bedroom Arlington townhome takes our crew roughly 2.5 to 3 hours, while a one-bedroom Clarendon high-rise condo usually runs about 1.5. Larger Colonials naturally take longer, and the difference is simply the added square footage and number of rooms. High-rise living in Rosslyn and Crystal City often means front-desk check-in, service elevators, and building certificate-of-insurance requirements, so we confirm those logistics before your appointment rather than discovering them at the door. Garden-apartment complexes and townhome rows tend to be more straightforward, though visitor parking still varies by community. Every clean begins with a free quote and is backed by our satisfaction guarantee. As a company that serves the entire DMV, we know Arlington's vertical, walkable neighborhoods well and plan each visit around how these buildings actually work.",
